# Slice 346 (the author 2026-11-10, LMX_blog/2026-11-10.md#colon-declares-not-assigns) and plan M11 5a (the author
# 2026-11-11): `Struct1: Struct2` is a declaration, not an assignment. Declared again, Struct1 is one more occurrence of
# the name -- its q w e r t stay -- and the second Struct1 holds the atom Struct2, not expanded: a path through it
# reaches the Structure Struct2 itself, with its a, b, c. The first three lines are the author's example; a bare
# Struct1 would be ambiguous, `data\[N]Struct1` selects an occurrence.
Struct2: a b c
Struct1: q w e r t
Struct1: Struct2
int: first length(data\[0]Struct1)
int: through length(data\[1]Struct1\Struct2)
